# Cloudflare reads this file instead of serving it. Every file in public/
# goes out with these headers. What worker.js answers itself (the API,
# pictures, the feed, the 404) sets its own.
#
#   nosniff             a file is only ever what its type says
#   Referrer-Policy     links off the site say which site, not which page
#   frame-ancestors     no other site can show these pages in a frame (the
#   X-Frame-Options     desktop framing its own windows is fine)
#   Permissions-Policy  nothing here needs the camera, the microphone or
#                       your location, so nothing gets them
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
